    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "the instr. or the nom. शिशुकैः—शिशव एव शिशुकाः । क expresses",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "pity. विधुरा—miserable ( दीना ). derived as विगता धूः कार्यभारो यस्याः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Lit. having nothing to do: hence perplexed, at a loss to know",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "what to do गद्गद &c.—Avy comp. दग्धजठरस्यार्थे—for the sake of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "the accursed stomach The word दग्ध is often used in the sense",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "it has here Cf. अस्य दग्धोदरस्यार्थे कः कुर्यात्पातकं महत् । H. I. See.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "notes on Nit. S'a. Sl. 99. मनस्वी a high-souled person; see",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "Nit. sl. 33.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 23. अभिमत०—highly valued. The demands of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "stomach make one completely forego all self-respect. गुरुतर—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "nobler; higher ग्राम—a collection. अम्भोज—the water lily that",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "blooms at sunrise, but fades when the mooon rises Cf. कुमुदवन-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "मपश्रि श्रीमदम्भोजखण्डं S'is. XI. 64. where the sun-rise is described.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "The moon-light-like जठरपिठरी makes the lotuses of virtues fade",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "away. विपुल०—विपुला ( विपुलं यथा तथा वा ) विलसन्ती या &c. कुठारिका",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "a small hatchet. पिठरी—a pan or boiler.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 24. पाली—the edge. सित &c –The edge of which is cover-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ed with a piece of white cloth. कपाली—a broken pot. न्याय &c.–",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "नयन्ति परमं पदं प्रापयन्ति विवेकेनेति न्यायाः श्रुतिशास्त्रस्मृत्यादयः says",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "Ràmarshi. The meaning here is ‘the formulæ or systems",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "manifested in the three Vedas’: the proper method of perform-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "ing sacrifices ). So this means क्रतुमन्त्राविनियोगविधिज्ञाः Malli.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "commenting on Kum. II 12 says नीयन्त एभिरर्थविशेषा इति न्यायाः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "स्वरास्तैरूदात्तानुदात्तस्वरितैः । This meaning will also do here—the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "Vedas pronounced correctly with proper intonation and accent).",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "धूम्र—of a smoky colour, blackened उपकण्ठम्—the adjacent part.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "द्वारं द्वारं प्रवृत्तः–-going to every door वरम्—an indecl. expressing",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "preference, and used with the clause containing the thing pre-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "ferred (which is put in the nom. case). See Apte's Guide § 301.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "तुल्यकुल्येषु–कुले भवाः कुल्याः fr कुल + यत् (य) by ‘दिगादिभ्यो’ यत्",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Pàn IV. 3. 54, कुल being a synonym of वंश. कुल्यः कुलोद्भवे मान्ये",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "कुलस्यातिहितेपि च । Vis'va. The sense intended by the poet,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "however, is तुल्यं च तत् कुलं तुल्यकुलं तत्र भवाः । But this is inadmis-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "sible from a grammatical point of view. भवार्थे यत् is to be added",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
